## Pattern 1, share 02: yes posts

### The parent asks what spoken communication should look like at this age and how to help it develop.

11 of 171 posts.

These posts ask about using words to converse, answer questions, describe the past or express needs, rather than only naming things or repeating memorized speech. Children range from just over two to three and a half, and the reported abilities range from no speech or single words to long sentences with limited back-and-forth, forgotten words, mixed pronouns or few questions. Some parents are seeking evaluations or home strategies; one says speech therapy is unaffordable, while another asks what to teach next to a child described as advanced.

- "My daughter is 3.5 years old. She knows all the colors. She knows how to say specific things such as shoes, socks, pants, hat, pizza, water, ice cream, lollipop.. and a few other single words. But she doesn’t talk in sentences. She still speaks in gibberish baby talk." [ar075-0114]
