Parents describe a two-year-old or nearly-three-year-old becoming harder to console, more aggressive, jealous, sleep-disrupted or newly demanding of milk after a baby arrives. They want to know whether the transition can be this severe, how to manage both children and whether professional help is needed. One parent of a three-year-old is anticipating these problems before the birth rather than reporting an existing regression.

- "I'm so overwhelmed and heartbroken. I feel awful for even thinking this, but a small part of me is almost regretting having a second. Not only do I feel like it has it caused all of this turmoil with my toddler, but I'm terrified of going through this stage a second time." [ar014-0031]
