- "I have a 2.5-year-old son and he is *constantly* on the move. He can’t really sit still unless he’s being actively engaged (like reading together or doing something hands-on). Otherwise he’s running, climbing, touching everything, talking to everyone… just full energy all the time." [ar078-0004]
- "Like sometimes I’m explaining instructions such as when we’re practising writing or learning something unsure quickly just space out again and I’ll ask her if she heard me and she didn’t notice. […] She’s not having an absent seizure or anything because she snaps out of it and I remember zoning out a lot as a kid as well and I think I’ve got ADHD." [ar021-0037]
- "When the TV is on, our toddler gets so into what he’s watching that when we talk or ask him questions, we have to repeat ourselves until he answers us half the time. He’s almost 3 years old - and he only watches it in the evenings after dinner, so I think it’s a combo of being tired & stimulated by the movie/ show." [ar034-0082]
- "Anyone else have 2 year old like this??? I feel like she is slightly delayed with speech, but only because she is CONSTANTLY on the move and has ZERO attention span. I am lucky if I can get through one line on one page of a book. I’ll ask her to repeat words or if she can say them… Nope in to the next thing. She is constantly climbing/exploring/ testing limits. She just will not sit still, and I feel like I can’t get her to listen to me or make eye contact because of this." [ar060-0122]
- "My point is that this age is an exhausting line between "Let them do it, they're learning" and "I want him to be entertained in a way that's not stressful for me or dangerous for him"." [ar015-0087]
