- "She says this every 10 minutes or less some parts of the day and gets very upset when we don't respond that we understand that she is a tiny tiny eencie weencie tiny baby." [ar046-0109]
- "I have tried giving him a fidget toy to hold instead, redirecting, saying “hands down” or “hands out of mouth” and it works for a minute and then he’s back to putting his hands in his mouth." [ar041-0107]
- "My 2-year-old has been rocking himself to sleep for a while now, but lately it has gotten a lot worse. He rocks back and forth pretty hard when he’s trying to fall asleep, sometimes repeatedly hitting his head against the wall/headboard. I moved his bed away from the wall, but he’ll still try to rock into whatever is behind him." [ar004-0130]

**But:** Some parents explicitly limit the concern to one pattern rather than reporting wider developmental difficulty. "It’s really just this, besides things that I can guarantee are typical." [ar056-0153]

