### The parent asks whether body curiosity or self-stimulation needs a response or a boundary.

6 of 171 posts.

Parents of children aged two to three and a half describe nipple or genital touching, public exposure, an apparently self-stimulatory pose called yoga, body-part jokes or requests, and genital details in a drawing. They want to know what is normal and how to teach privacy or respond without shame; some worry about what other adults may infer or whether the child could have experienced inappropriate touch. The posts include both repetitive physical behaviour and language or drawings that surprised the adult.

- "I have a 26 months old, who, for the past month has been constantly touching her nipples. The minute her hands are idle she just puts her hand inside her top and puts them on her nipples. she seems to do it absent-mindedly but if I tell her to put her hands away, she refuses to do so." [ar015-0010]
- "Well now I got a memo that he exposed himself at daycare. He took down his pants and underwear and showed his privates to his peers." [ar006-0059]
- "My almost 3-year-old has started doing a pose where she kind of lays on the floor and clenches her legs together and pushes forward on her other leg.  She says she's doing yoga, but I suspect it's self-stimulatory in some way." [ar020-0082]
- "He said this morning mommy you have such a big butt, it’s like a drum. Mind you I thought it was hilarious. But then tonight he said mommy I love your body. I love your vagina." [ar047-0045]
- "Today he drew a penis on his robot, came over to be to point to where it is on me(if I had one) and then told me he drew a penis." [ar077-0125]
- "One night while I was kissing her face/head, she said “kiss my \[vulva\],” then “kiss my butt,” and laughed. I told her we don’t kiss private parts and redirected her." [ar073-0130]

**But:** The parent distressed by private-body-part requests also explicitly reports no disclosure of touching, kissing or hurting, no named person or secrets, and easy redirection. "She’s otherwise happy and behaving normally. She is only ever left alone with close family. She hasn’t said anyone touched/kissed/hurt her there, hasn’t identified a person or talked about secrets, doesn’t seem distressed when talking about it, and is easily redirected." [ar073-0131]

