These posts concern failed hearing and vision screens in a distressed two-year-old, possible teething or constipation at unknown ages, appetite at three, recurring leg pain at three, and trousers that seem too long for an almost-two-and-a-half-year-old. Parents ask whether tests or bodily changes mean a problem, a growth spurt or ordinary learning and development. The clothing question is about fit and proportions, while the leg-pain account describes medicine, unsuccessful massage and plans for an appointment.

