- "Normal gums or early teething?" [ar044-0018]
- "Bear with me here. I've got a very average height almost 2.5 year old, 53rd percentile. He doesn't have a long torso, he's proportionally more leg than upper body. But I have not found a single pair of toddler pants that aren't too long on him. We're mostly ok with elastic bands at the bottom, and lots of shorts in the hot weather, but jeans and loose leg pants are all way too long. Are these just made for extra extra long legged kids? Do their legs have a separate growth spurt that we just haven't hit yet?" [ar001-0063]
- "How to tell if my baby is constipated? We’ve just started solid food and now he poops a bit less often and he seems to be struggling when pooping. I’m hoping it’s just a learning curve since the poop is more solid now and he may have to push a little harder than he’s used to. I just hope he’s not stopped up 😔" [ar043-0073]
- "I don't know if it's a growth spurt or what but lately my 3 year old has a ravenous appetite. On top of her 3 usual meals she's now wanting 3-4 snacks a day." [ar073-0119]
- "I assumed it was growing pains, but it's been going on quite a while and it's only ever the left side. I remember my legs hurting a lot when I was young, usually the left side as well, but never enough to make me cry like that. It did last for years though, not months." [ar047-0074]

**But:** The parent describing failed screening explicitly reports no earlier concern about either sense, and says the child is meeting developmental milestones. "I’ve NEVER had any concerns about his hearing or vision. I’m probably a little more anxious about meeting milestones than most, but vision or hearing issues were never on my radar for him and I never noticed any red flags." [ar049-0001]

